==Strategy==
Killerwatts initially appear as passive floating orbs of electricity, and once clicked will '''immediately''' grow limbs and become hostile. If the player attacked the killerwatt from within melee range, the killerwatt will continue to attempt to get into melee range until it dies, the player leaves the [[Killerwatt plane]], dies, or logs off. Killerwatts are much more dangerous than their [[combat level]] may suggest, as both their [[Ranged]] and [[Melee]] attacks have an [[attack speed]] of two ticks, which is twice as fast as the player (with most weapons).

There are two recommended ways to fight killerwatts, depending on equipment and preference:

# Range the killerwatts from at least two tiles away. They will still launch [[magical ranged]] attacks, but won't be able to move into melee range. [[Protect from Missiles]] prevents damage from these attacks, or  armour with high magic defence like [[dragonhide armour]] can be worn to mitigate it. [[Air spells]] are also effective, taking advantage of the monsters' 60% [[elemental weakness]].
# Click them with a melee weapon equipped then walk away before the attack lands, making the killerwatt path toward the player and engage first. This will force it to attack using only melee, with [[Protect from Melee]] preventing all damage. When using this technique, it is advisable to turn run off and to click a killerwatt that is quite far away, giving more time to click away from the monster and stand still while it approaches and lands the first hit.

Using these techniques, all the killerwatt's attacks can be mitigated using protection prayers. If choosing not to pray against their attacks, [[insulated boots]] decrease damage significantly.

